			"type": "text",
			"text": "Litorosuchus was an archosauriform from Falang Formation of People's Republic of China, dating back to the Early Cretaceous. Its name is a combination of 'litoral' as in the part of the sea shore close to the land and 'suchus' meaning crocodile. It was a medium sized animal being about 2 meters long with a tail taking up more than half of its length. There is one nearly complete specimen laying on its side known, helping us with what we know about it."
